 "notes": "Eot-Wash rotating spin-pendulum axion-wind search on the electron. Curve traced (yellow/green boundary = black 95% CL Rice limit) from Fig.5 bottom panel (fig5cmerged: equilibrium halo model, v_a = XY component of v_sun, |v_a|=240 km/s), the headline result shown with astro comparisons; the X- and Y-direction panels (top/middle) are similar. Paper reports limit on C_e/F_a in PeV^-1 with L = C_e (d_mu a/2F_a) e-bar gamma^mu gamma_5 e, i.e. F_a=f_a. Converted to canonical g_ae = C_e m_e/f_a = m_e*(C_e/F_a), m_e=5.10999e5 eV, so g_ae[dimensionless] = (C_e/F_a [PeV^-1]) * 5.11e-10. Flat part ~0.5-0.7 PeV^-1 matches abstract F_a/C_e>2e15 eV (=0.5 PeV^-1). Features: sidereal bump near 47 zeV, high-mass rise from finite-duration attenuation. dm density 0.45 GeV/cm^3 (limit scales with assumed density via a_tilde_0); not rescaled.",
